This page defines false discovery proportion, false discovery rate, and
family-wise error rate for a fixed finite testing family, then specifies the
Benjamini–Hochberg step-up rule. Under mutual independence of all p-values and
exact Uniform$(0,1)$ true-null p-values, a leave-one-out identity gives the
exact FDR $(m_0/m)q$. False-null p-value laws may be arbitrary subject to the
stated independence. The result concerns FDR, not FWER; dependent tests and
discrete superuniform true-null extensions require separate arguments.
